First off: I want to thank everyone who contributes to RGRN and writes
the guides, FAQs, spoilers, etc. I play Wiz-Elf-Mal-Cha and my last two
games have been much more successful thanks to what I'm learning--mostly,
to slow down!

My most recent death however came as quite a surprise. I made it down
to the Medusa level for the first time. I had +oExtraHeal, but lesson
learned: that won't help if you've completely drained your Pw with
attack & enchant spells during battle. :-) Better carry ! next time.

The titan was casting Aggravate and Summon Nasties; the latter wasn't too
bad since I had +oCharmMonster to make them switch to my team. Something
was hitting me with a hooked polearm (which I guess I have learned is
a ranged weapon, since only friendlies were adjacent). I finally waited
for a gap in the crowd and used a /oDeath charge to dispatch the titan,
and let the pets kill everything else off.

I was cleaning up after the battle, standing on the up-stairs, and
suddenly:

Strike one: My pet winged gargoyle attacks me. I play with hilite_pet
turned on and it was still showing in reverse-video, but I used ; to
double-check ... yep, "tame".

Strike two: Tried throwing food to no effect; gargoyle hits me again. I
made this guess because the only time I've ever had a pet (tame creature)
attack me is when it's hungry. Lesson learned: Should have immediately
read up on the winged gargoyle, to learn that it doesn't eat.

Strike three, you're out: After poring over my inventory for options
(among other conclusions: no way to heal myself, no teleport), and too
soon to pray, I decided to head upstairs. Too late did it occur to me
that since it's a pet, of course it would come with me. The gargoyle
hits me; DYWYPI?

All the above of course means I am *still* not thinking long enough when
in danger. :-) But my immediate question is: What caused the gargoyle
to attack me? I can only think of three things it could have been:

1. The titan's casting of Aggravate (mentioned earlier). Can this affect
pets? Or, if a monster was aggravated before I charmed it to be my
pet, can that effect linger somehow? If either of these is true, that
creates an unfortunate situation; can't kill a tame creature attacking
you without angering Anhur. (Incidentally: How long does it take before
aggravate-monster wears off?)

2. My knowledge of the "charm monster" spell was growing faint as I was
using it. Does that weaken the spell somehow? (I re-read the spl spoilers
and see no mention of this.)

3. Could one of the summoned I turned into a pet have been wearing
=oConflict? The rint spoiler says even pets may attack in this case.

As far as other things I could have tried: would an engraved-Elbereth
square have helped in this case; will a tame creature that's attacking me
(for reasons other than food) respect Elbereth?

Charming is currently my favorite Wiz ability, and I am interested in
shaping part of my playing style around it, so I want to make sure I
figure out what happened here so I can beware in the future. Thanks for
any insight; spoilers welcome!

